  "body": {
    "id": "prop:common-union-support-ancestry",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "On an input generated by \\(\\mathfrak M_{p,m}^{\\mathrm{pub}}\\), the relation \\(\\mathcal A_G(\\mathcal O_G)\\) is exactly the set of ordered pairs \\((i,j)\\) for which \\(i\\) is an ancestor of \\(j\\) in the union-support DAG of every tuple in \\(\\Theta_G(\\mathcal O_G)\\). Given the exact-once tuple stream, it is computable by exact zero tests, transitive closure, and intersection in \\(O(N_{\\mathrm{out}}(mp^2+p^3))\\) additional time and \\(O(p^2)\\) working space beyond the tuple being processed.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "M_pub",
      "p",
      "m",
      "Anc_G",
      "O_G",
      "i",
      "j",
      "Theta_G",
      "N_out"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:common-union-support-ancestry",
      "def:identified-tuple-set",
      "def:modified-cholesky",
      "thm:published-all-orders-covariance-compatible"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "By \\(\\texttt{thm:published-all-orders-covariance-compatible}\\), the output\nset is nonempty. For \\(T\\in\\Theta_G(\\mathcal O_G)\\), choose\n\\(\\pi\\in\\mathfrak S_V\\) with \\(T=T_\\pi\\). The construction in\n\\(\\texttt{def:modified-cholesky}\\) places a nonzero entry\n\\(B_\\pi^{(a)}[j,i]\\) only when \\(i\\) precedes \\(j\\) in \\(\\pi\\). Every\nedge of \\(\\mathcal U(T)\\) therefore points forward in \\(\\pi\\), so\n\\(\\mathcal U(T)\\) is acyclic and its strict transitive closure is precisely\nits ancestry relation.\n\nBy \\(\\texttt{def:common-union-support-ancestry}\\), an ordered pair belongs\nto \\(\\mathcal A_G(\\mathcal O_G)\\) exactly when it belongs to every one of\nthese strict transitive closures. This proves the characterization. To\ncompute it, inspect the \\(m p^2\\) coefficient entries of each tuple using\nexact zero comparisons, compute reachability in \\(O(p^3)\\) operations, and\nintersect the resulting \\(p\\times p\\) Boolean relation with the running\nintersection. Reusing the same two Boolean matrices gives \\(O(p^2)\\)\nworking space and total additional time\n\\(O(N_{\\mathrm{out}}(mp^2+p^3))\\).",
    "justification": "The proposition restores the promised ancestry deliverable as a direct, non-novel exact computation from the emitted tuples.",
    "gap": "The tuple enumerator alone does not name the common causal-order information needed by the parent workflow.",
    "consumer": "The workflow receives the ancestry relation shared by every covariance-compatible coefficient mechanism.",
